\tag{fdip}
\title{Reflection forms for coupled matter}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A positive determinant weights ordinary connection configurations,
while a reflected matter insertion also probes the signed exterior
coefficient. Can the two resulting reflection forms have different
signs? A finite Hermitian test makes the distinction explicit on the
two-cell time circle, where the vertices are exchanged and both edges
meet the reflection boundary.}

